1. FIX THE VERIFIED CYPRESS SEED REGRESSION
Current exact-head Cypress Parity fails before Cypress launches. Both Chrome and Firefox fail at `Validate seeded Cypress database` because the new lossless-id64 system `9007199254740993` is intentionally non-eligible (`has_body_data=false`, `body_count=0`) but the workflow's blanket ratings top-up inserts a rating for every system. `data_invariants.py --target-rating-version 3.4` then correctly reports `Non-eligible with rating: 1` and stops.

Fix the seed/top-up logic so ratings are created only for systems that satisfy the repository's real eligibility contract. Do NOT weaken/skip data invariants, do NOT special-case by hiding the unsafe id64 from tests, and do NOT make the deliberately lossless-id64 row falsely eligible by inventing body data. Preserve its exact decimal id64 and its purpose in the product journey. Add/adjust a focused contract test so future blanket rating top-ups cannot recreate stale non-eligible ratings.

After this fix the normal Product E2E lane must actually boot the API/apps/web and execute the newly added V3 Explore -> Babylon -> Inspect tests in Chrome and Firefox.

2. PRODUCT E2E REMAINS THE NORMAL USER-BEHAVIOUR AUTHORITY
Keep Cypress Product E2E separate from Review Lab. Product E2E runs apps/web + Babylon against normal seeded API/data and owns normal user journeys and approved V3 visual assertions. Cypress validates product behaviour, not source code. Do not move generic lint/type/security/code-review checks into Cypress.

Confirm the current first-checkpoint journey really runs after the seed fix: Explore usable; search/typeahead finds seeded systems; lossless id64 survives; result/map selection stays synchronized; Inspect loads canonical detail; renderer resize/remount produces no uncaught error; accessibility smoke passes. Preserve Chrome + Firefox. Old React screenshots/layout are not V3 visual authority.

3. RETARGET REVIEW LAB TO APPS/WEB + BABYLON
